      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose:\n- **Immediate-release:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Extended-release:** the maximum is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which may be what you intended.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- Another dose. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
      }
